  "outstanding": [
    "The coordinate translation theorem for large-gap discrete series is derived through the embedding of a shifted model (RSI-06), and the existence and identification of their coefficient models through the kernel realization (KRL-05). The compact Weyl dimension formula, the coefficient limit and its global integrable envelope remain named source inputs at this depth.",
    "The source also gives a separate lowest-compact-type upper bound. Only the lower half enters this part of Count5. The compact signatures and small gaps do not occur in this particular argument.",
